---
title: "contract_upgrade::authorize_upgrade (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_seq: sequence = governance::take_sequence(receipt)
    q_seq --> q_check_seq: sequence > last_executed_governance_sequence
    q_check_seq --> q_abort: false, abort E_CANNOT_EXECUTE_WITH_OBSOLETE_SEQUENCE
    q_check_seq --> q_update: true
    q_update --> q_digest: set_last_executed_governance_sequence_unchecked(pyth_state, sequence)
    q_digest --> q_take: digest = take_upgrade_digest(receipt)
    q_take --> q_handle: handle_upgrade_contract(pyth_state, digest)
    q_handle --> [*]: return state::authorize_upgrade(pyth_state, digest)

    note right of q_update
        INV-001: uses _unchecked variant (no LatestOnly needed for upgrade path)
        INV-002: sequence replay protection same as other governance actions
        INV-003: digest must be non-zero bytes
        INV-004: governance action must be CONTRACT_UPGRADE type
        INV-005: target_chain_id must not be 0 (upgrade is chain-specific)
    end note
